 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-11-02 (44): Wolf packs (NOT b1.7.3). Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run (+1 test `wolves_come_in_packs_on_a_quota_of_their_own`, `wolves_are_born_in_forests_taigas_and_groves` extended; every number UNVERIFIED by eye). Why a player saw none: one animal try in 21 gave a wolf, only when the one ring cell was `Forest` / `Taiga` / grove, out of the 12 places all animals shared, and the Blooming woods were not in `wolf_land` at all. Now: `wolf_land` adds `SeasonalForest` (a `BiomeGenForest` in b1.7.3 too) and the Blooming `AutumnalForest`, `OakWoodland`, `WetWoodland`; wolves have `CAP_WOLVES` 8 around the player and no longer count in `CAP_ANIMALS` / `CAP_KIND` (new `FARM`); `Mobs::spawn` makes a wolf try of its own on 1 in `WOLF_ONE_IN` (6) animal ticks, in `wolf_land`, no other wolf within `WOLF_APART` (32); `pack` makes 3..=5 wolves and gives each member three tries. ponytail: the pack only spawns together, it does not keep together after (no follow-the-leader AI); wild wolves still despawn like any mob (`Mob::old`).
 - 2026-11-02 (43): Bone meal on blocks (`missing.md` 8). Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+1 test `gear::tests::bone_meal_seeds_only_empty_cells_above_grass`). `ItemDye.onItemUse` damage 15, in the block-use path of `lib.rs` before `ItemSeeds`: sapling (6) -> `ChunkManager::grow_tree` with the species `meta & 3` (the Java's `growTree`; the item is used up even when the tree does not fit); crops (59) -> metadata 7 (`BlockCrops.fertilize`); grass (2) -> `gear::bone_meal_grass`, the 128 random walks of the Java (`i / 16` steps, a walk dies off the grass or in a normal cube; an empty end cell gets tall grass meta 1 at 9 in 10, else a dandelion 2 in 3 or a rose), drawing from the item's own `Random` (`mobs.rng`). Anything else: no use, nothing consumed. No sound (the Java has none). ponytail: an unloaded cell reads as stone, so a walk into it just ends; the sapling uses `mobs.rng` where the Java passes `world.rand` (same distribution, other stream).
 - 2026-11-01 (42): Four quality-of-life features without a new meter (`design.md` "QoL without a new meter"). Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device; every number and every pixel UNVERIFIED (+6 tests: `biomelife::tests::{the_overlay_tint_follows_the_air, the_almanac_counts_to_dusk_and_names_the_day}`, `combat_hud::tests::the_marks_come_in_a_fixed_order_and_stay_in_their_squares`, `items::tests::a_death_pile_lasts_four_times_as_long_and_is_found`, `map::tests::the_death_cross_is_pinned_in_the_arrows_units_and_held_at_the_edge`, `book::tests::a_chest_near_the_bench_lends_its_ingredients_to_the_book`; `mend::tests` gains one assert). All four only with the Immersive Pack ON (`combat::rules::on`), NOT b1.7.3, no new switch.
     - **Gauges**: `biomelife::tint(Air)` colours the stamina's grey overlay warm in the heat and cool in the cold; `combat_hud::{Mark, marks, draw_marks}` draw up to four 5 x 5 pixel marks right of the tenth heart (sun, frost, a bandage's cross, the hearth's flame) from `Air`, `Mend::bandaged` and the new `Mend::hearth_on`; read in `build_hud` before `hud_verts` is borrowed. No state, no toggle.
